{{also|hit-up|hitüp}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|hit<,,hit> up}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To contact with a [[request]] or [[demand]].
#: {{syn|en|touch base}}
#: {{ux|en|Why not '''hit him up''' for some assistance on the rebuilding project?}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[talk]] with (someone) about a [[desire#Verb|desired]] [[subject]].
#: {{syn|en|chat up}}
#: {{ux|en|I'd like to '''hit him up''' about last episode, but he's working all night.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To take an intoxicating drug.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|hit it up}}
* {{l|en|HMU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|rugby}} The act of taking a pass from the [[dummy-half]] and running straight into the opposition's defensive line without looking to pass.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|hitup}}
* {{l|en|hit-up}}

